# EigenScript gap: at most 255 live cooperative tasks (the handle table
# threads, channels, tasks and stores share; docs/CONCURRENCY.md). EigenLua
# runs each coroutine as a task, so a program holding more than about 250
# suspended coroutines at once fails where Lua (no such limit) does not.
# Not a #1286 row; a VM limit.
# Lua:  local t = {} for i = 1, 1000 do t[i] = coroutine.create(coroutine.yield)
#       coroutine.resume(t[i]) end print(#t) -> 1000
# Expected: 1000 suspended tasks (or a limit far above Lua programs' needs).
# Actual 686d3b7d: "task_spawn: too many live tasks (max 255)", then 255
# Rows: cstack.lua (line 105, "chain of 'coroutine.close'") (S).
define parked(x) as:
    task_recv of null
    return null
n is 0
try:
    for i in range of 1000:
        task_spawn of parked
        n is n + 1
catch e:
    print of e.message
print of n
